  "body": "Part of #372. Lifts the #374 refusal of probing on an inverted X/Y, for Fanuc. Haas follows when its probing hooks land (PR #360), hence `Refs #392`.\n\n## What changed\n- **Translation.** `post::invert` mirrors the probing records on an inverted X/Y, the same way it mirrors a move. It negates the TOUCH target and expected trip, the RETREAT back-off delta and its end point, and each FOUND axis's expected value.\n- **New manifest flag `probeAxisInversion = true`.** The translation runs only for a post script that declares it, and only `fanuc.cps` does. Haas declares `axisInversion` but not this flag, so it refuses probing by name. Posts without `axisInversion` already refuse any inverted machine.\n\n**Why negating is right.** The controller position is `M = G54 + P`, and the tip stands at `S·M`, where S = −1 on the inverted axis.\n- The posted `P = S(W − origin)` lands correctly only if G54 holds `S·D`.\n- A part off by d trips at `S(W_trip + d − origin)`. The translated expected value is `S(W_trip − origin)`, so the deviation is `S·d`.\n- `G10 L2 X[#5221+dev]` then gives `S(D + d)`: the real part's datum in controller coordinates.\n- Back-offs are increments, so they flip with the axis. `ABS[dev]` and the choice of travel axis are sign-free.\n- In full: `docs/decisions/392-probe-inverted-axis.md`.\n\n## How tested\nNew `inverted_probe` (8 tests). The posted Fanuc programs run on a **test-only macro-B controller** (`crates/app/tests/macro_b/`): G31 trips where the stylus first meets a simulated part, every G0/G1 is collision-checked, and unmodelled words are errors.\n- **Physical offset:** face −Z, face −X, edge −Y, corners +X+Y and −X−Y, bore and boss, each on standard, inverted-X, inverted-Y and inverted-XY machines, with the part shifted (0.37, −0.21, −0.13) mm.\n  - G55 always ends at the physical datum, within 0.002.\n  - G54 is untouched, and unmeasured axes aren't written.\n  - The standard machine gives the same answer, which checks the interpreter.\n- **Edge cases:** a part exactly on the model returns the datum unchanged. No contact raises `#3000=2`, and out of tolerance raises `#3000=1`.\n- **Converse checks:** the untranslated program misses on an inverted machine. Undoing any one translated word breaks it: a stylus crash, a tolerance alarm, or probing past overtravel.\n- **Both sign forms:** the reader accepts the old `#100--2.5` and the folded `#100+2.5` from #386, which is now on main. Re-run after merging main: 8/8.\n- **Existing suites:** `inverted_post`, `inverted_equivalence`, `axis_direction`, `probe_op`, `probe_reach`, `fanuc_post`, `conformance` and the camcraft-post suites pass. **No golden changed.** `clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` passes except #415, which is red on main.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo run on a real control with an inverted axis. The macro interpreter proves the arithmetic and motion of the posted words.\n\nChangelog: Probing posts on a Fanuc machine with an inverted X/Y axis (the probe records are mirrored like moves; the written work offset is the physical correction) (#392)\n\nRefs #392\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
